      "raw_response": "# 7-Day MVP Plan: AI Contract Review Assistant\n\n## Recommended stack\n\n- **Frontend:** Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui\n- **Backend:** Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, Pydantic\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL 16 on Amazon RDS\n- **File storage:** Amazon S3\n- **Queue:** Amazon SQS\n- **Workers:** Python worker running on ECS Fargate\n- **Authentication:** Clerk\n- **LLM:** OpenAI API using a fast model for extraction/classification and a stronger model for final review\n- **Document parsing:** PyMuPDF, python-docx, mammoth; AWS Textract as an OCR fallback\n- **Frontend hosting:** Vercel\n- **Backend hosting:** Amazon ECS Fargate\n- **Infrastructure:** Terraform\n- **Monitoring:** Sentry, CloudWatch, structured JSON logs\n\nThe MVP should focus on reliable document ingestion, clause-level review, explainable findings, and a useful report. It should not attempt to automatically rewrite entire contracts or provide jurisdiction-specific legal advice.\n\n---\n\n# 1. System architecture\n\n## High-level components\n\n```text\nBrowser\n  |\n  | HTTPS\n  v\nNext.js Frontend on Vercel\n  |\n  | Clerk authentication\n  |\n  | REST API calls\n  v\nFastAPI API on ECS Fargate\n  |\n  +--> PostgreSQL/RDS\n  |\n  +--> S3 document storage\n  |\n  +--> SQS processing queue\n  |\n  +--> OpenAI API\n  |\n  +--> AWS Textract for OCR fallback\n  |\n  +--> Sentry and CloudWatch\n             ^\n             |\n      Review Worker on ECS Fargate\n```\n\n## Data flow\n\n### Contract upload\n\n1. User signs in through Clerk.\n2. Frontend requests a presigned S3 upload URL from the API.\n3. API verifies the user’s organization membership and creates a `documents` row.\n4. Browser uploads the original PDF or Word file directly to S3.\n5. Browser calls a completion endpoint.\n6. API verifies the object exists and submits a message to SQS.\n7. The worker processes the document asynchronously.\n\n### Document processing\n\n1. Worker downloads the