      "raw_response": "# MVP objective\n\nBuild a multi-tenant web application where legal-team users can:\n\n1. Upload `.pdf` or `.docx` contracts.\n2. Extract and normalize contract text.\n3. Identify standard clauses and missing clauses.\n4. Flag risks against a configurable playbook.\n5. Generate suggested replacement language.\n6. Review findings with citations to the source.\n7. Export a summary report as PDF or DOCX.\n\nThe MVP should position all AI output as proposed analysis requiring human review.\n\n---\n\n# 1. System architecture\n\n## Technology choices\n\n- **Frontend:** TypeScript, Next.js 15, React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui\n- **Backend:** Python 3.12, FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic\n- **Background jobs:** Celery with Redis\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL 16 with `pgvector`\n- **File storage:** Amazon S3\n- **Authentication:** Supabase Auth\n- **Document parsing:** PyMuPDF, `python-docx`, Amazon Textract fallback\n- **AI provider:** OpenAI API with structured JSON output; provider abstraction for later model changes\n- **Report generation:** WeasyPrint for PDF and `python-docx` for DOCX\n- **Deployment:** Vercel, Render, Supabase, AWS S3/Textract, Upstash Redis\n- **Monitoring:** Sentry, OpenTelemetry, structured JSON logs\n\n## Components\n\n### Web application\n\nThe Next.js application handles:\n\n- Login and invitation acceptance\n- Organization and playbook management\n- Contract uploads\n- Job progress\n- Contract viewer\n- Finding review\n- Report generation and download\n\nThe browser never receives permanent S3 credentials. It requests a short-lived presigned upload URL from the backend.\n\n### FastAPI service\n\nThe API handles:\n\n- JWT validation\n- Tenant authorization\n- Upload initialization and completion\n- Contract metadata\n- Findings and review actions\n- Playbook configuration\n- Report generation\n- Audit events\n- Presigned S3 download URLs\n\n### Background worker\n\nA Celery worker handles long-running operations:\n\n1. Validate uploaded file.\n2. Scan and inspect the file.\n3. Extract text.\n4. Run OCR if necessary.\n5. Normalize paragraphs and page references.\n6. Segment the document.\n7. Extract clauses.\n8. Compare clauses against the playbook.\n9. Generate risk findings and redlines.\n10. Store results and update progress.\n11. Generate summary reports when requested.\n\n### Data flow\n\n```text\nBrowser\n  |\n  | Supabase login -> JWT\n  |\n  | POST /uploads/presign\n  v\nFastAPI --------------------------> PostgreSQL\n  |\n  | presigned PUT URL\n  v\nBrowser --------------------------> S3\n  |\n  | POST /contracts/{id}/process\n  v\nFastAPI -> Redis/Celery queue -> Worker\n                                  |\n                                  +-> S3: download original\n                                  +-> PyMuPDF/python-docx\n                                  +-> Textract if OCR is required\n                                  +-> LLM API\n                                  +-> PostgreSQL: clauses/findings/results\n                                  +-> S3: generated reports\n\nBrowser polls GET /contracts/{id}/status or receives SSE progress events.\n```\n\n## Repository layout\n\n```text\ncontract-review/\n  apps/\n    web/                  # Next.js application\n    api/                  # FastAPI application\n    worker/               # Celery tasks and processing pipeline\n  packages/\n    schemas/              # Shared JSON schemas and generated TS types\n    prompts/              # Versioned AI prompts\n    playbooks/            # Default playbook definitions\n  infrastructure/\n    terraform/            # S3, IAM, Textract-related resources\n  tests/\n    fixtures/             # Sanitized test contracts\n    golden/               # Expected clause and finding results\n  docker-compose.yml      # Local Postgres, Redis, API and worker\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. Database schema\n\nUse UUID primary keys, UTC timestamps, and organization-scoped queries. Enable PostgreSQL row-level security for defense in depth.\n\n## `organizations`\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | Primary key |\n| `name` | VARCHAR(200) | Organization name |\n| `slug` | VARCHAR(100) | Unique |\n| `settings` | JSONB | Retention and AI settings |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n| `updated_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n\n## `users`\n\nSupabase Auth owns credentials; this table stores application profile data.\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | Matches Supabase Auth user ID |\n| `email` | CITEXT | Unique |\n| `full_name` | VARCHAR(200) | |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n| `last_seen_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n\n## `organization_members`\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `organization_id` | UUID | Foreign key |\n| `user_id` | UUID | Foreign key |\n| `role` | ENUM | `owner`, `admin`, `reviewer`, `viewer` |\n| `status` | ENUM | `invited`, `active`, `disabled` |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n\nPrimary key: `(organization_id, user_id)`.\n\n## `playbooks`\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | Primary key |\n| `organization_id` | UUID | Tenant |\n| `name` | VARCHAR(200) | |\n| `contract_type` | VARCHAR(100) | `nda`, `msa`, `dpa`, `other` |\n| `description` | TEXT | |\n| `is_default` | BOOLEAN | |\n| `version` | INTEGER | |\n| `created_by` | UUID | User |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n| `updated_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | |\n\n## `playbook_rules`\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | Primary key |\n| `playbook_id` | UUID | Foreign key |\n| `clause_type` | VARCHAR(100) | Example: `limitation_of_liability` |\n| `title` | VARCHAR(200) | |\n| `required` | BOOLEAN | Flag if missing |\n| `preferred_position` | TEXT | Human-readable rule |\n| `fallback_position` | TEXT | Acceptable compromise |\n| `severity` | ENUM | `low`, `medium`, `high`, `critical` |\n| `redline_template` | TEXT | Optional approved wording |\n| `rule_config` | JSONB | Structured thresholds and conditions |\n| `sort_o