nerates a summary report and stores it as a JSON blob in the `reports` table.\n8. The frontend polls `GET /contracts/{id}/analysis` or receives a WebSocket event (MVP: polling) to update the UI.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Database Schema\n\n**Database:** PostgreSQL (via Supabase). All tables use UUID primary keys and timestamps.\n\n### Tables\n\n**organizations**\n| Field         | Type                     | Description                  |\n|---------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|\n| id            | UUID PK                  |                              |\n| name          | string                   | Company name                 |\n| created_at    | timestamp                |                              |\n\n**users**\n| Field         | Type                     | Description                  |\n|---------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|\n| id            | UUID PK                  | Supabase Auth UID            |\n| email         | string                   |                              |\n| org_id        | UUID FK → organizations  |                              |\n| role          | enum('admin','member')   |                              |\n| created_at    | timestamp                |                              |\n\n**contracts**\n| Field         | Type                     | Description                  |\n|---------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|\n| id            | UUID PK                  |                              |\n| org_id        | UUID FK → organizations  |                              |\n| uploaded_by_id| UUID FK → users          |                              |\n| filename      | string                   |                              |\n| s3_key        | string                   | File path in S3              |\n| file_size     | integer                  | bytes                        |\n| status        | enum('uploaded','processing','completed','failed') | |\n