le from R2 → extracts text (PDF/Word) → normalizes into pages/sections.\n5. Worker calls LLM pipeline:\n   - Clause extraction (structured JSON)\n   - Risk classification per clause\n   - Redline suggestions\n   - Executive summary + risk score\n6. Results written to DB (`clauses`, `risks`, `redlines`, `reports`); contract `status=ready`.\n7. Frontend polls or uses SSE/WebSocket-lite (or just React Query refetch) → shows review UI.\n8. User can accept/edit redlines (MVP: view + export only; light edit optional).\n9. User downloads summary report (Markdown/PDF generated server-side).\n\n**Key design choices for 7 days:**\n- Synchronous API only for light ops; heavy work always async.\n- Single-tenant-per-org model (org_id on every row).\n- Idempotent jobs keyed by `contract_id`.\n- Strict Pydantic schemas for all LLM outputs.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Database Schema (PostgreSQL)\n\n**Tables (concrete):**\n\n```sql\n-- organizations\nid              UUID PK\nname            TEXT NOT NULL\nslug            TEXT UNIQUE\nplan            TEXT DEFAULT 'mvp'\ncreated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ\n\n-- users (synced from Clerk or local mirror)\nid              UUID PK\nclerk_id        TEXT UNIQUE\nemail           TEXT UNIQUE\nfull_name       TEXT\norg_id          UUID FK → organizations\nrole            TEXT  -- 'admin' | 'reviewer' | 'viewer'\ncreated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ\n\n-- contracts\nid              UUID PK\norg_id          UUID FK\nuploaded_by     UUID FK → users\ntitle           TEXT\nfilename        TEXT\nfile_key        TEXT          -- R2 object key\nfile_type       TEXT          -- 'pdf' | 'docx'\nstatus          TEXT          -- uploaded|processing|ready|failed\npage_count      INT\nchar_count      INT\nerror_message   TEXT\ncreated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ\nupdated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ\n\n-- contract_text (raw extracted text, optional chunking)\nid              UUID PK\ncontract_id     UUID FK\npage_number     INT\ncontent         TEXT\ntoken_estimate  INT\n\n-- clauses\nid             