      "raw_response": "# MVP Plan: AI Contract Review Assistant (\"Clause\")\n**Constraint:** 7 calendar days, 3 engineers. Goal is a *pilot-ready* product for 2–5 friendly design-partner legal teams, not a GA launch.\n\n**Pre-requisite (do this before Day 1 — it is not optional):** collect 15–25 real (or realistic) contracts in the target category (pick ONE: mutual NDAs + SaaS MSAs) and secure ~2 hours/day of a lawyer SME. Without a labeled golden set and a domain expert, the AI stages cannot be tuned and you will ship something plausible-looking and wrong. Narrowing to two contract types is the single biggest scope decision that makes 7 days feasible.\n\n**Team allocation**\n- **E1 — Backend/AI:** FastAPI, job pipeline, LLM stages, prompt engineering, evals.\n- **E2 — Frontend:** Next.js app, document viewer, review workspace, report UI.\n- **E3 — Full-stack/Infra:** auth, tenancy, ingestion/parsing/OCR, exports, deploy, CI, observability.\n\n---\n\n## 1. System Architecture\n\n**Components**\n\n1. **Web app (Next.js 15, App Router, TypeScript)** — deployed on Vercel. Server components for shell/lists, client components for the review workspace. Talks only to the API over HTTPS with a Clerk-issued JWT.\n2. **API service (Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn/Gunicorn)** — stateless HTTP layer. Validates JWT, enforces tenancy, issues presigned upload URLs, enqueues jobs, serves read models. Deployed on Render as a Web Service.\n3. **Worker service (Celery 5 + Redis broker)** — same codebase, different entrypoint. Runs the multi-stage document pipeline. Deployed on Render as a Background Worker (2 replicas, concurrency 4).\n4. **Postgres 16 + pgvector (Neon)** — system of record: orgs, users, contracts, clauses, findings, redlines, reports, audit log. pgvector stores embeddings for playbook-rule retrieval.\n5. **Redis (Upstash)** — Celery broker/result backend, rate limiting, idempotency keys, short-lived job status cache.\n6. **Object storage (Cloudflare R2, S3-compatible)** — original uploads, normalized text JSON, generated PDF/DOCX artifacts. Private buckets; all access via presigned URLs with 15-min TTL.\n7. **LLM providers** — Anthropic API (Claude Sonnet 4.5 for reasoning-heavy stages, Claude Haiku 4.5 for cheap classification), OpenAI `text-embedding-3-small` for rule embeddings. Provider access is behind an internal `LLMClient` abstraction so a fallback can be swapped in.\n8. **OCR fallback** — AWS Textract `DetectDocumentText` (async) for scanned PDFs.\n9. **Auth (Clerk with Organizations)** — hosted sign-in, org creation, invites, roles. FastAPI verifies JWTs via JWKS.\n10. **Observability** — Sentry (app errors, both tiers), Langfuse (LLM traces/cost/eval), Axiom (structured logs), BetterStack (uptime).\n\n**Data flow (happy path)**\n\n```\nBrowser\n  1. POST /v1/contracts            -> API creates contract row (status=awaiting_upload)\n                                      + returns presigned R2 PUT URL\n  2. PUT <presigned url>           -> file lands in R2 (raw/{org_id}/{contract_id}/original.pdf)\n  3. POST /v1/contracts/{id}/process -> API validates object exists, creates job row,\n                                        enqueues Celery chain, returns 202\n  Worker chain (each link is a checkpointed Celery task, idempotent, retried):\n     ingest  -> normalize text + char offsets (+ OCR branch)\n             -> segment into clause candidates (deterministic + LLM repair)\n             -> classify clause types (Haiku, batched)\n             -> retrieve playbook rules (pgvector) + classify risk (Sonnet)\n             -> generate redlines for findings above severity threshold (Sonnet)\n             -> compute server-side word diffs\n             -> generate executive summary (Sonnet, map-reduce)\n             -> render report artifacts (PDF via WeasyPrint, DOCX via python-docx)\n             -> set contract.status = ready, write audit log\n  4. Frontend polls GET /v1/contracts/{id}/job (2s interval, exponential backoff)\n  5. GET /v1/contracts/{id}/review -> single payload: pages, clauses, findings, redlines\n  6. User accepts/edits redlines    -> PATCH /v1/redlines/{id}\n  7. POST /v1/contracts/{id}/report -> re-render with accepted redlines, return presigned download\n```\n\n**Why polling not WebSockets:** one less moving part, works through Vercel/Render defaults, and a 60–180s job doesn't justify the socket infrastructure in week one. Server-Sent Events is a 2-hour upgrade later.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Database Schema\n\nPostgres 16, SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM, Alembic migrations. **Every tenant-scoped table carries `org_id` and every query goes through a repository layer that requires it.**\n\n```sql\n-- ============ Tenancy & identity (mirrored from Clerk) ============\nCREATE TABLE organizations (\n  id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  clerk_org_id    TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  name            TEXT NOT NULL,\n  plan            TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pilot',\n  risk_threshold  SMALLINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 3,   -- min severity to auto-generate redline\n  monthly_doc_quota INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 200,\n  created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  clerk_user_id TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  email         CITEXT NOT NULL,\n  full_name     TEXT,\n  created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE memberships (\n  org_id  UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  role    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('owner','admin','member','viewer')),\n  PRIMARY KEY (org_id, user_id)\n);\n\n-- ============ Documents ============\nCREATE TABLE contracts (\n  id                UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  org_id            UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  created_by        UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n  title             TEXT NOT NULL,\n  contract_type     TEXT,                -- 'nda' | 'msa' | 'unknown'\n  counterparty_name TEXT,\n  our_role          TEXT,                -- 'customer' | 'vendor' | 'discloser' | 'recipient'\n  status            TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'awaiting_upload',\n                    -- awaiting_upload|queued|processing|ready|failed|archived\n  source_filename   TEXT,\n  mime_type         TEXT,\n  file_bytes        BIGINT,\n  page_count        INT,\n  storage_key_raw   TEXT,                -- r2://raw/{org}/{contract}/original.pdf\n  storage_key_text  TEXT,                -- normalized text JSON\n  overall_risk_score NUMERIC(4,2),       -- 0.00-10.00\n  ocr_used          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n  deleted_at        TIMESTAMPTZ,\n  created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ix_contracts_org_created ON contracts(org_id, created_at DESC)\n  WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;\n\nCREATE TABLE contract_pages (\n  id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  org_id      UUID NOT NULL,\n  contract_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES contracts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  page_number INT NOT NULL,\n  char_start  INT NOT NULL,   -- offset into full normalized text\n  char_end    INT NOT NULL,\n  width_pt    NUMERIC(8,2),\n  height_pt   NUMERIC(8,2),\n  text        TEXT NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE (contract_id, page_number)\n);\n\n-- ============ Pipeline jobs ============\nCREATE TABLE processing_jobs (\n  id             UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  org_id         UUID NOT NULL,\n  contract_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES contracts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  celery_task_id TEXT,\n  status         TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued',  -- queued|running|succeeded|failed|cancelled\n  current_stage  TEXT,   -- ingest|segment|classify|risk|redline|summary|report\n  stages_done    JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n  progress_pct   SMALLINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  attempt        SMALLINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n